    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Imagine walking through a quiet Australian grassland. Suddenly, you hear a tiny, strange “Ooom” sound. That sound might belong to one of the rarest birds in the world—the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Plains-wanderer",
            "zh": "领鹑"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "! Scientists in Australia have just used Artificial Intelligence (AI) to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "locate",
            "ref": "v-locate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " these birds. This discovery will help protect the endangered birds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Plains-wanderers are very "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "picky",
            "ref": "v-picky"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " about where they live. These tiny birds live in grasslands, but not just any grasslands. There can’t be too much grass or too little. For this reason, scientists sometimes call them the “Goldilocks*” of animals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "They used to be common in eastern Australia. But over the years, farms and cities have taken over their home. Now, there are only 250 to 1,000 birds left in the wild. The birds are tiny, only about 15 centimetres tall, and they don’t fly well. When they feel frightened, they "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "crouch",
            "zh": "蹲伏"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to hide or run rather than fly. “There is no bird like it in the world,” said a scientist. In fact, scientists have even put the species into a “family” all by itself, since there are no other similar birds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "To protect these rare birds, scientists first needed to know where they were. They worked together and decided to “listen” for the birds. Female Plains-wanderers make an unusual “Ooom” sound, and this was the key to locating them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The researchers set up 35 recording devices to catch these sounds. The devices collected tens of thousands of hours of recordings. Humans couldn’t check all of it, so the team used AI to help. The AI detected calls from two locations, and scientists later "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "confirmed",
            "ref": "v-confirm"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the findings. One scientist said it felt like “finding gold”. It is the first time in over 30 years that the bird has been found west of Melbourne."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, scientists will work with landowners to protect these birds and their grasslands. And they are still listening, hoping to find even more of these “Goldilocks” birds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*Goldilocks：童话人物金凤花姑娘，比喻“适中、刚好”。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
